We need to express: if 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) then for all int i; 0 <= i && i < index; the element at position i after add is either same as before, or if it was null before then still null. Actually "remains unchanged or continues to be null if it was null before" meaning: if old element at i was null, then after add it's still null; else it stays unchanged (i.e., equals old). That's basically: this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)). Since null equality: if old is null, then this.get(i) should be null as well, which is same as equality. So we can just assert equality. But need to consider that after insertion, elements shift? In ArrayList.add(index, element) inserts element at index, shifting subsequent elements to the right. So elements before index remain unchanged. So equality works.

